Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Hygiene.wlt", "Section",
 CellID->493634489],

Cell["\<\
Tests for desc evaluation-hygiene and the string axis tier (feat/desc-hygiene).

The desc eDSL must distinguish three uses of the same surface syntax: a \
binder
`a_` (an axis to be solved), a bracket `#a` = Slot[\"a\"] (a named op-axis), \
and a
bare `a` (env capture \[LongDash] evaluates to its value UNLESS its name is \
an established
axis identity, then a hygienic reference).  A globally shadowed axis symbol \
(a
`Block[{c=3},...]`) must not leak its value into an axis identity.  A string \
`\"a\"`
(valid identifier) is the fully-hygienic axis spelling.

Run via: wolframscript -script scripts/run-tests.wls
BeginTestSection/EndTestSection are MUnit markers; the runner loads MUnit`.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->958996842],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Einstoff`DescHygiene", "Subsection",
 CellID->807242762],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[",
  RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", "c", ",", "k", ",", "r", ",", "n"}],
  "]"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellID->133430704],

Cell["Fixtures.", "Text",
 CellID->839445067],

Cell["x23 = {{1,2,3},{4,5,6}} ; x24 = {{1,..,4},{5,..,8}}", "Text",
 CellID->104519553],

Cell["\<\
1. HEADLINE: a shadowed binder must not capture its value.  Today this is \
$Failed
(the `{s}` extraction re-evaluates c -> 3); it must equal the unshadowed swap.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->488889079],

